    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1083">

                <pb facs="1437" n="1427" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6461/5–445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of State,
                        at San Francisco</hi><anchor n="11a" xml:id="d1083-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-04">May 4, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>31. Understand Chinese Minister of Foreign Affairs may approach you in regard to
                    assistance of this Government, particularly the Bureau of Reclamation, in
                    connection with Yangtze Gorge hydroelectric power project. This matter is now
                    under consideration in the Department and attitude of interested divisions, as
                    far as determined, <pb facs="1438" n="1428" xml:id="pg1428"/> apparently not
                    favorable. Clayton<anchor n="12" xml:id="d1083-f2"/> will be prepared to discuss
                    the question with you and Minister Soong.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1083-f1" n="11a" type="source" xml:id="d1083-f1-content">
                <p>Mr. Stettinius was attending the United Nations Conference at San Francisco.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1083-f2" n="12" xml:id="d1083-f2-content">
                <p>William L. Clayton, Assistant Secretary of State for Economic Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
